From: Alex Chong <achong@meta.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Feb 2026 12:54:57 -1000
Subject: [PATCH 34/63] disable audio through webrtc for qemu vmm

Summary:
# Motivation:
Streamer webrtc component wants to setup audio with qemu, but currently we only want to use it for the extended controls.

https://www.internalfb.com/code/aosp-device-google-cuttlefish/[<internal-branch>%3Aa431b4408c26fb46fe710a3904897f54d3927661]/host/commands/run_cvd/launch/streamer.cpp?lines=152-157

## error:
```
CF_EXPECT(audio_server_->IsOpen(), audio_server_->StrError())
```

# Overview:
- remove audio from streamer for QEMU until we can get display working

Test Plan:
# Build Host Tools
```
. build/envsetup.sh
lunch aosp_cf_arm64_phone-userdebug
m out/host/darwin-x86/cvd-host_package.tar.gz
```

# Pull gw
```
device sf device
device virtual -t device
```

# Replace Host Tools:
```
 rm -r bin com.android.i18n lib64 nativetest64/ framework etc usr
 ln -s  /Volumes/AOSP/out/host/darwin-x86/cvd-host_package/* .
```

# Launch
```
./start_cuttlefish.py
```

